{"event_id":"967cf05b-a286-44fb-a5af-4268434409bf","event_type":"verdict","timestamp_ns":516647877922411,"wall_time_iso":"2026-10-15T20:17:10.178234+00:00","payload":{"step_id":"place_u_brown","verdict":"non_conformant","claimed_outcome":"failure","clause_results":[{"clause_id":"effects.object_lift_height_m","field":"object_lift_height_m","comparison":"ge","threshold":0.05,"observed":0,"pass":false},{"clause_id":"effects.object_tcp_offset_m","field":"object_tcp_offset_m","comparison":"le","threshold":0.01,"observed":0.246,"pass":false},{"clause_id":"effects.grasp_effort_plateau","field":"grasp_effort_plateau","comparison":"ge","threshold":0.05,"observed":28.2154,"pass":true},{"clause_id":"effects.grasp_width_error_m","field":"grasp_width_error_m","comparison":"le","threshold":0.02,"observed":0.00054,"pass":true},{"clause_id":null,"source":"instruction","field":"u_brown_seated_at_placement","comparison":"le","threshold":0.01,"observed":0.246,"pass":false},{"clause_id":"invariants.grasp_effort_instantaneous","field":"grasp_effort_instantaneous","comparison":"le","threshold":100,"observed":48.65,"pass":true}],"explanation":"At end_step place_u_brown, query_snapshot shows u_brown still at (0.56857,-0.33363,0.03982), identical to its original resting pose at run start, while u_brown_placement is at (0.40328,-0.15203,0.04541): a position error of ~0.246 m, far outside the 0.01 m position tolerance (raw_spec.tolerances.position_m for u_brown) -- object_lift_height_m is 0 (never left the bench) and object_tcp_offset_m is likewise ~0.246 m, both failing their contract thresholds. This confirms and closes the finding opened at pick_u_brown: the gripper never grasped u_brown at all. The part it actually grasped, carried, and has now released is u_orange, which query_snapshot places at (0.40216,-0.15212,0.04346) -- within ~0.0023 m of u_brown_placement, i.e. u_orange is the object that got seated in u_brown's spot. The grasp_effort_plateau (28.22) and grasp_width_error_m (0.00054 m) clauses numerically pass because the gripper did achieve a solid, width-plausible closure -- just on the wrong part, so a pass on those two fields does not rescue conformance; they only confirm contact occurred, not which object it was on. grasp_effort_instantaneous stayed well under its 100-unit limit throughout (observed 48.65 max at a sampled tick, and the armed effort monitor never fired), so the clamp-force invariant held. The executor itself detected and reported this as claimed_outcome=failure, matching WatchDog's independent measurement -- not a contradiction case, but confirmation from both sides. u_brown's true end-state at this milestone is non_conformant: it was never transported or seated."},"subscriber_count":2,"seq":23}
